<section class='slide main-slide'>
  <div class='main-slide__inner'>
    <div class='main-slide__copy'>
      <p class='main-slide__eyebrow'>Open-source realtime server · in production since 2017</p>
      <h1 class='main-slide__title' id='pro'>Every message arrives.</h1>
      <p class='main-slide__subtitle'>
        AnyCable keeps WebSocket connections open through your deploys and replays what a client missed when it comes back online. Delivery guarantees, ordering and presence, built in.
      </p>
      <p class='main-slide__stack'>
        For Rails, FastAPI, Laravel, Node.js, and any backend that can send an HTTP request.
      </p>
      <div class='main-slide__ctas'>
        <a href="https://plus.anycable.io" target="_blank" class='button button_size_big main-slide__cta plausible-event-name=Signup plausible-event-location=hero' data-ph-capture-attribute-link-id='start-managed'>
          Start free on Managed AnyCable
        </a>
        <a href="/#pricing" class='main-slide__cta-secondary plausible-event-name=Navigation plausible-event-link=hero-pro' data-ph-capture-attribute-link-id='self-host-pro'>
          Self-host Pro →
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class='main-slide__note'>
        Managed AnyCable is free for one instance. Pro has a 2-month trial, no card needed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class='main-slide__stage live-map' data-controller='live-map'>
      <canvas class='live-map__canvas' data-live-map-target='canvas' role='img' aria-label='Live map of connections: your app broadcasts through the AnyCable server to about a hundred client devices. Simulated network drops, deploys and traffic spikes show missed messages replaying from stream history.'></canvas>
      <div class='live-map__hud'>
        <div class='live-map__switch' role='group' aria-label='Realtime server'>
          <button type='button' class='live-map__switch-btn' data-live-map-target='mode-any' aria-pressed='true'>AnyCable</button>
          <button type='button' class='live-map__switch-btn live-map__switch-btn_ws' data-live-map-target='mode-ws' aria-pressed='false'>In-process WebSockets</button>
        </div>
        <dl class='live-map__tally'>
          <div class='live-map__tally-item'><dt>delivered</dt><dd data-live-map-target='delivered'>0</dd></div>
          <div class='live-map__tally-item live-map__tally-item_ok'><dt>replayed</dt><dd data-live-map-target='replayed'>0</dd></div>
          <div class='live-map__tally-item'><dt>lost</dt><dd data-live-map-target='lost'>0</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class='live-map__bar'>
        <div class='live-map__actions'>
          <button type='button' class='live-map__action live-map__action_primary plausible-event-name=Demo plausible-event-action=tunnel' data-live-map-target='tunnel'>Drop the network</button>
          <button type='button' class='live-map__action plausible-event-name=Demo plausible-event-action=deploy' data-live-map-target='deploy'>Deploy the app</button>
          <button type='button' class='live-map__action plausible-event-name=Demo plausible-event-action=spike' data-live-map-target='spike'>Launch-day spike</button>
          <span class='live-map__auto' data-live-map-target='auto'>autoplay · press a button to take over</span>
        </div>
        <div class='live-map__log' data-live-map-target='log' aria-live='polite'></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ul class='main-slide__stats'>
    <li class='main-slide__stat'><b>100%</b><span>of messages delivered through Wi-Fi drops</span></li>
    <li class='main-slide__stat'><b>0 s</b><span>reconnect storm when you deploy</span></li>
    <li class='main-slide__stat'><b>3 ms</b><span>p50 roundtrip at 10K connections</span></li>
    <li class='main-slide__stat'><b>18 KB</b><span>RAM per idle connection on Pro</span></li>
    <li class='main-slide__stat main-slide__stat_link'>
      <a href="/compare/nodejs-websocket" class='plausible-event-name=Navigation plausible-event-link=hero-benchmark' data-ph-capture-attribute-link-id='hero-benchmark'>Measured in our 2026 benchmark against Socket.io and uWebSockets.js →</a>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
